Done. Pipeline complete.

**Result: OOF AUC 0.59131** — LogisticRegression(C=0.02) on 5 features `[loading, measurement_17, m3_na, m5_na, measurement_2]`, leave-one-product-out GroupKFold, per-product rank normalization postprocess.

Key findings:
- Train products A–E vs test F–I disjoint. GroupKFold by product_code mandatory. Simple LR generalizes better than shallow LGBM (0.5906 vs 0.5842 raw OOF) — trees overfit per-product noise.
- measurement_17 Huber-imputed per product from 4 most-correlated measurements; m3/m5 missingness indicators carry signal (fail rate 0.160/0.254 vs base 0.213).
- Per-product rank normalization: consistent +0.0007 across all 40 sweep configs (pooled AUC penalizes cross-group distribution shift).
- LR+LGB blend +0.00002 — noise level, rejected per experience prior.

